==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|ljúka}}, {{m|non|lúka}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*lūkaną|*leukaną, *lūkaną|t=to shut, lock}}. Of the two forms, ''ljúka'' and ''lúka'', the latter is attested earlier.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈljuːka/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|uːka|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|lauk|luku|lokið}}

# to [[finish]], to [[end]] {{+obj|is|dat}}
# to [[complete]] {{+obj|is|dat}}
# to [[end]], to [[close]], to come or bring to an end {{+obj|is|dat}}
# to [[finalise]]/[[finalize]] {{+obj|is|dat}}
# {{lb|is|of a|limited period of time}} to [[expire]] {{+obj|is|dat}}
# to [[conclude]] {{+obj|is|dat}}

